Special quest monsters are not limited to 120, but I believe this lack
of checking only applies on the quest itself.  I could be wrong about
that, though.  Also, monsters which would normally be extinct can
still be summoned via the monster spell summon nast(y|ies).

It's pretty widely accepted that, if you cast create monster on every
level of the gnomish mines, main dungeon and gehennom and cannot
generate any monsters, you have most likely extincted all the
extinctable monsters.  For bonus points, feel free to try and extinct
NOGEN monsters, like woodchucks, and others which need special
terrain, like sea monsters (giant/electric eels, piranha, jellyfish,
etc.)  Cursed ?oGeno and /oUT are your friends here!

